+---
+
+## Draft mutation receipts and recovery
+
+- `draft update` and `draft revise` carry `expectedUpdatedAt`. An explicit
+  `--if-unmodified-since` is the user's reviewed version; otherwise fetch the version before writing.
+  A 409 must never trigger an automatic read-and-retry with a newer version.
+- `revise` requires a caller-supplied stable request ID. Retrying an uncertain result must preserve
+  the request ID, patch and target; do not generate a replacement key automatically.
+- A transport failure or HTTP 5xx after a mutation does not prove rollback. Replace the generic
+  unavailable hint with readback/replay instructions; retain the error status and nonzero exit code.
+- Successful mutation receipts retain all server fields and add environment/source/result IDs and
+  status. Missing draft identity/status or `affectsPublishedContent: false` is a contract error,
+  with readback guidance because the mutation may already have committed.
